            "type": "paragraph",
            "location": {
              "line": 3,
              "heading": "How to Start Your Aventro Car"
            },
            "text": "Starting your Aventro car is a simple process, but exact procedures may vary slightly depending on the model, fuel type, and technology (conventional, electric, or hybrid). Below is a general step-by-step guide for Aventro Petrol, Diesel, Hybrid, and Electric cars."
          }
        ],
        "sections": [
          {
            "title": "For All Aventro Models",
            "level": 2,
            "location": {
              "line": 7,
              "heading": "How to Start Your Aventro Car"
            },
            "blocks": [],
            "sections": [
              {
                "title": "1. Ensure Safety First",
                "level": 3,
                "location": {
                  "line": 9,
                  "heading": "For All Aventro Models"
                },
                "blocks": [
                  {
                    "type": "list",
                    "location": {
                      "line": 10,
                      "heading": "1. Ensure Safety First"
                    },
                    "ordered": false,
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "text": "Sit in the driver’s seat and fasten your seatbelt.",
                        "depth": 0
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Ensure the gear lever is in 'P' (Park, for automatic) or 'N' (Neutral, for manual).",
                        "depth": 0
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Press the brake pedal (and the clutch for manual transmission).",
                        "depth": 0
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ],
                "sections": []
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "title": "A. Petrol & Diesel Models",
            "level": 2,
            "location": {
              "line": 16,
              "heading": "How to Start Your Aventro Car"
            },
            "blocks": [],
            "sections": [
              {
                "title": "With Standard Key Ignition",
                "level": 3,
                "location": {
                  "line": 18,
                  "heading": "A. Petrol & Diesel Models"
                },
                "blocks": [
                  {
                    "type": "list",
                    "location": {
                      "line": 19,
                      "heading": "With Standard Key Ignition"
                    },
                    "ordered": true,
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "text": "Insert the Key:",
                        "depth": 0
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Insert the car key into the ignition slot (usually on the right of the steering column).",
                        "depth": 1
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Turn the Key:",
                        "depth": 0
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Turn the key clockwise to the \"ON\" position (dashboard lights turn on).",
                        "depth": 1
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Continue turning to the \"START\" position. Release when the engine starts.",
                        "depth": 1
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ],
                "sections": []
              },
              {
                "title": "With Push-Button Start",
                "level": 3,
                "location": {
                  "line": 25,
                  "heading": "A. Petrol & Diesel Models"
                },
                "blocks": [
                  {
                    "type": "list",
                    "location": {
                      "line": 26,
                      "heading": "With Push-Button Start"
                    },
                    "ordered": true,
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "text": "Ensure Key Fob is Inside the Car:",
                        "depth": 0
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "The key fob should be in your pocket or bag within the vehicle.",
                        "depth": 1
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Press the Start/Stop Button:",
                        "depth": 0
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Press and hold the brake pedal.",
                        "depth": 1
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Press the \"Start/Stop\" button. The engine will start.",
                        "depth": 1
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ],
                "sections": []
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "title": "B. Electric Models",
            "level": 2,
            "location": {
              "line": 34,
              "heading": "How to Start Your Aventro Car"
            },
            "blocks": [
              {
                "type": "list",
                "location": {
                  "line": 36,
                  "heading": "B. Electric Models"
                },
                "ordered": true,
                "items": [
                  {
                    "text": "Key Fob Present",
                    "depth": 0
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Ensure the key fob is inside the vehicle.",
                    "depth": 1
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Press Brake Pedal",
                    "depth": 0
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Firmly press and hold the brake pedal.",
                    "depth": 1
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Press Start Button",
                    "depth": 0
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Press the \"Start/Stop\" button. Indicator lights and systems will activate.",
                    "depth": 1
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Ready Indicator",
                    "depth": 0
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Wait for the 'READY' signal/light on the dashboard. The car is now ready to drive silently.",
                    "depth": 1
                  }
                ]
              }
            ],
            "sections": []
          },
          {
            "title": "C. Hybrid Models",
            "level": 2,
            "location": {
              "line": 47,
              "heading": "How to Start Your Aventro Car"
            },
            "blocks": [
              {
                "type": "list",
                "location": {
                  "line": 49,
                  "heading": "C. Hybrid Models"
                },
                "ordered": true,
                "items": [
                  {
                    "text": "Key Fob Present",
                    "depth": 0
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Make sure the key fob is with you, inside the car.",
                    "depth": 1
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Press Brake Pedal",
                    "depth": 0
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Press and hold the brake pedal.",
                    "depth": 1
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Press Start Button",
                    "depth": 0
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Press the \"Start/Stop\" button.",
                    "depth": 1
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "The car may start silently in EV mode or with a slight engine sound in engine mode. Watch for 'READY' signal on the dashboard.",
                    "depth": 1
                  }
                ]
              }
            ],
            "sections": []
          },
          {
            "title": "Additional Tips",
            "level": 2,
            "location": {
              "line": 59,
              "heading": "How to Start Your Aventro Car"
            },
            "blocks": [
              {
                "type": "list",
                "location": {
                  "line": 60,
                  "heading": "Additional Tips"
                },
                "ordered": false,
                "items": [
                  {
                    "text": "For all models, ensure all warning lights turn off after starting.",
                    "depth": 0
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Do not press the accelerator while starting.",
                    "depth": 0
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "For electric/hybrid, if 'READY' does not appear, try restarting.",
                    "depth": 0
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "quote",
                "location": {
                  "line": 66,
                  "heading": "Additional Tips"
                },
                "text": "If you're unsure or the car doesn't start, refer to your Aventro user manual or contact the nearest Aventro Service Center."
              }
            ],
            "sections": []
          }
        ]
